.TH PCBGERBER 1
.SH NAME
pcbgerber \- write the Gerber and drill files of a board
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pcbgerber
[
.B \-L
.I lib
] ...
.B \-o
.I dir
.I board.pcb
.RI < board.lock
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Pcbgerber
writes into
.I dir
one RS-274X file for each copper layer, named after it (top.gbr,
in1.gbr, ..., bottom.gbr), the outline (edge.gbr), the top solder mask
and paste (topmask.gbr, toppaste.gbr), the silkscreen of each side
(topsilk.gbr, bottomsilk.gbr), the outlines of the courtyards
(topcourt.gbr, bottomcourt.gbr, a drawing only) and the Excellon
drill file (drill.drl), in mm.
The silkscreen is each footprint's silk lines and its part's
designator, by its courtyard where it is clear (see
.IR pcbcheck (1)),
read from below on the bottom, and cut where the mask opens.
A plane layer is the outline 0.3 mm in, cleared by the clearance round
every hole, via, pad and track not of its net, and round each pad of
its net that it relieves (a small part's of two pins), which joins it by
its neck.
Each pad carries its part's name (TO.C) and each object its net (TO.N);
a plane is one region under its net.
.SH EXAMPLES
pcbgerber -o gerber ch1.pcb < ch1.lock
.SH SEE ALSO
pcb(5), gbrvec(1)
